Z||000000||sqoach||10-28-2001||08:02 PM||||I hadn't driven it for a while, and it had gotten a little colder out. But it's been colder and I had no problems. It started fine, but then it did the idle "search" and went too low, then died. I started it up again and went up the road to a light...died again...started up...died...started up and stayed on the gas a bit. Then it did ok after it warmed up some. What does this mean? My volts are good. Battery is good. Fuel filter was change a couple months ago. Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||9
