Z||000007||ChopTop||11-02-2001||10:34 AM||||Just got off the phone with my mechanic.  He's replacing the engine control module, plus the crank sensor.  He said the sensor was cracked and leaking OHMs.  He also replaced the fuel filter.  When we first took it to him he couldn't get it to stall, which made it difficult for him to diagnose.  It stalled on him this time hence the above repairs.  He said he's 99% sure he found the problem.  If it stalls again he'll be replacing the fuel pump located in the gas tank.  <BR>Sqoach, did you figure out your car's problem?||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||11-02-2001||01:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>Just got off the phone with my mechanic.  He's replacing the engine control module, plus the crank sensor.  He said the sensor was cracked and leaking OHMs.  He also replaced the fuel filter.  When we first took it to him he couldn't get it to stall, which made it difficult for him to diagnose.  It stalled on him this time hence the above repairs.  He said he's 99% sure he found the problem.  If it stalls again he'll be replacing the fuel pump located in the gas tank.  <BR>Sqoach, did you figure out your car's problem?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Haven't found the problem yet, but I haven't really been looking. It hasn't died on me since then, so I'm not sure what happened.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||reddog||11-02-2001||06:58 PM||||Coolant Temperature Sensor????<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||I'mSmall||11-03-2001||12:36 AM||||I one time had a problem with a Cavalier(imagine that) where after driving it until it reached normal operating temperatures, when I would go to stop it would stall and not start until it had sat for a while and was cool. If you have on automatic transmission, you may be having this problem. The problem is a sensor in the transmission went out. This sensor is for the low 3rd gear. If you unplug this sensor(it's on the outside of the transmission toward the front of the car) it won't stall any more but you wont have the low/overdrive, but this will allow you to drive it until you get a new sensor. ||||reg||3
